{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall take this staff in your hand, with which you shall perform the signs</b> — The staff has not yet been mentioned, only one sign, that it will become a serpent (Exodus 4:3). Rather, it means: <b>with which you shall perform the signs</b> — which I will tell you. And it appears to me that when HaShem said to Moses, \"in all My wonders which I will perform in its midst\" (Exodus 3:20), He informed him of them in detail, but the verse shortens. And this is the meaning of <b>with which you shall perform the signs</b>."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:02:38.350133014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}